</style><h2>Blinky 1.5.20</h2><ul><li><strong>Grok 的主账号在命令行登录失效后仍显示用量。</strong> 在「设置 → Grok」把「用量来源」留在「自动」时，Blinky 先用命令行登录；这份登录缺失、过期或被拒绝（401 或 403）时，改用在「Grok 账号」一行点一次「登录…」保存的设备码登录，并且不写入 <code>~/.grok/auth.json</code>。<a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/pull/81">#81</a></li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/releases/tag/v1.5.20">在 GitHub 查看更新说明</a></p>]]></description>
            <description xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<style>
  h2 { font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0 0 .5em; }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  li { margin: .3em 0; }
  p { margin: .8em 0 0; }
</style><h2>Blinky 1.5.20</h2><ul><li><strong>The primary Grok account keeps showing usage after the CLI login expires.</strong> With Read usage from left on Automatic under Settings → Grok, Blinky uses the CLI token first and, when that token is missing, expired, or refused (401 or 403), the device-code login saved by Sign in once on the Grok account row, and does not write <code>~/.grok/auth.json</code>. <a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/pull/81">#81</a></li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-mac/releases/tag/v1.5.20">Release notes on GitHub</a></p>]]></description>
